      "The blur rides the motion: <code>stdDeviation = sin(πt) × 5</code>, zero at rest, because a standing alpha-contrast blur smears neighbouring colours into one gradient. Because each swatch is one solid colour at every frame, the filter can only ever bridge the gap between two — which is liquid.",
